{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMU8iXtqfGCjGX3Cyix1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0179L6bvuZDFGVnrbrV1d9us","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add reports/R7/accept.sh && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nR7 accept.sh: real capped socket wait + identity-field normalisation\n\nInstrument-only commit, no code, per operator CEVAP (a) in\nreports/kosu/6.operator.md. The 1000 us ceiling is NOT touched.\n\n1. sock_bekle(): the readiness loops at GOAL 2a and 2b spun `seq 50` with\n   no sleep -- ~2-3 ms total, most of it the seq fork -- while a daemon\n   needs 21.8-22.6 ms to bind and a minimal reference daemon lost 10/10\n   to that loop. The loop timed a race, not a daemon. The socket stays\n   MANDATORY; only the wait becomes real, capped at 10 s.\n\n2. kimliksiz(): GOAL 3 compared runId (\"ng-<ms>-<pid>\", gate.cpp:2738),\n   the sandbox-derived `pipe`, and the real project path in the refusal\n   text. No honest implementation can pin a pid, and normalising the path\n   inside the gate would print the user a directory that does not exist,\n   so the blanking belongs in the instrument. Exit code, ev, mode, rule,\n   refusal text and ledger line count/order are still compared byte for\n   byte; the chain hash is NOT blanket-blinded.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit accept.sh change alone"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":616,"cache_read_input_tokens":80874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":616},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baed5e1f-1a03-43c7-ba0d-e3a68687202c","uuid":"a11378d5-f1bd-423b-b93a-09d28e39aba8","request_id":"req_011CeMU8hkGMyV3hvKdVUpYc"}
