{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MHt94L6Uyj2vJLaY2zfMS8","type":"tool_result","content":"CHALLENGE.md\nDENEMELER.md\nHARNESS.md\nTESHIS.md\naccept.out\naccept.sh\n=== last deneme ===\n5:## deneme 1 — 2026-08-24 (tur 1, yapan) — teşhis turu, kod yazılmadı\n56:## deneme 3 — 2026-08-24 (tur 6, yapan) — daemon YAZILDI, iki fail-open bulundu ve kapatıldı, hız iddiası ÇÜRÜDÜ\n=== SONUC/CHALLENGE files ===\nreports/R7/CHALLENGE.md\nreports/R7/DENEMELER.md\nreports/R7/HARNESS.md\nreports/R7/TESHIS.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baed5e1f-1a03-43c7-ba0d-e3a68687202c","uuid":"732c3527-b9ef-485e-89a5-ba8b0c65bc8e","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:10:31.559Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"CHALLENGE.md\nDENEMELER.md\nHARNESS.md\nTESHIS.md\naccept.out\naccept.sh\n=== last deneme ===\n5:## deneme 1 — 2026-08-24 (tur 1, yapan) — teşhis turu, kod yazılmadı\n56:## deneme 3 — 2026-08-24 (tur 6, yapan) — daemon YAZILDI, iki fail-open bulundu ve kapatıldı, hız iddiası ÇÜRÜDÜ\n=== SONUC/CHALLENGE files ===\nreports/R7/CHALLENGE.md\nreports/R7/DENEMELER.md\nreports/R7/HARNESS.md\nreports/R7/TESHIS.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMUH1y79xj7uQNCoUDDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QD5MF2QSVFcugfBvJRZrfU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/reports/R7/LENGTH.md","content":"# R7 — residual length dependence, re-measured with the daemon up\n\nMeasured 2026-08-24 by `reports/R7/accept.sh` GOAL 2c. Every number below is\ncopied from the run, not computed by hand (Law 7); the raw run is\n`reports/R7/accept.out`.\n\n## Instrument\n\nThe R1.3 in-process probe: a COPY of `native/gate.cpp` patched under `/tmp`\nwith a `steady_clock` stamp at the top of `main()` and an `atexit` dump, built\nthere. `native/` is never touched. Two sandboxes are seeded — one to 50\nevents, one to 400 — BOTH before EITHER is timed, then the two are called\ninterleaved, one after the other, 250 times each, so clock drift and machine\nload land on both arms in the same millisecond.\n\n## Numbers\n\n| session length | in-process median |\n|---|---|\n| 50 events  | 1665.8 us |\n| 400 events | 1748.8 us |\n\n**Divergence: 4.98%.**\n\nCompanion number from GOAL 2b, same run, same instrument: the overall\nin-process median with the daemon up is **1704.4 us over 300 samples**,\nagainst R7's 1000 us ceiling. That is RED. See `reports/R7/DENEMELER.md`\ndeneme 4.\n\n## What it means, honestly\n\nR1.3 closed this at 3.5–4.9% under a 10% ceiling, with process spawn IN the\ndenominator. The prediction written into `accept.sh` was that removing spawn\nshrinks the denominator, so the same absolute cost must read as a LARGER\npercentage. It did not grow the way that prediction implies — 4.98% sits at\nthe top of R1.3's band, not above it.\n\nThe reason is visible in the 2b number and should not be spun into good news:\nthe denominator did not shrink. The median under the daemon is 1704.4 us,\nwhich is not a post-spawn cost. `native/gated.cpp` forks TWICE per request,\nso the design that was measured re-pays a process cost the daemon was\nsupposed to delete. Until that is addressed, 2c's percentage is being taken\nagainst a denominator that still contains process creation, and it is\ntherefore NOT the re-measurement R1.3 asked for. The number is recorded\nbecause the plan requires it to be carried forward; it is not evidence that\nthe length dependence is under control.\n\nAddress named, not fixed here: `reports/R1.3/PROFIL.md:229,277` puts\n`save#2` at ~165 us and attributes the residual to `last_ledger_mode()`'s\nwhole-file fallback being O(file).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1091,"cache_read_input_tokens":90175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1091},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baed5e1f-1a03-43c7-ba0d-e3a68687202c","uuid":"e73d93b2-aa28-4a11-89c6-28a9cb2fdff6","request_id":"req_011CeMUGzaGTUhojD82xrhE2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QD5MF2QSVFcugfBvJRZrfU","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/reports/R7/LENGTH.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baed5e1f-1a03-43c7-ba0d-e3a68687202c","uuid":"ff320ca0-f7f0-4e26-a6ac-62495cfaf6d0","timestamp":"2026-08-24T11:10:45.967Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/damummyphus/damla_projects_2026/rabadon-kosu2/reports/R7/LENGTH.md","content":"# R7 — residual length dependence, re-measured with the daemon up\n\nMeasured 2026-08-24 by `reports/R7/accept.sh` GOAL 2c. Every number below is\ncopied from the run, not computed by hand (Law 7); the raw run is\n`reports/R7/accept.out`.\n\n## Instrument\n\nThe R1.3 in-process probe: a COPY of `native/gate.cpp` patched under `/tmp`\nwith a `steady_clock` stamp at the top of `main()` and an `atexit` dump, built\nthere. `native/` is never touched. Two sandboxes are seeded — one to 50\nevents, one to 400 — BOTH before EITHER is timed, then the two are called\ninterleaved, one after the other, 250 times each, so clock drift and machine\nload land on both arms in the same millisecond.\n\n## Numbers\n\n| session length | in-process median |\n|---|---|\n| 50 events  | 1665.8 us |\n| 400 events | 1748.8 us |\n\n**Divergence: 4.98%.**\n\nCompanion number from GOAL 2b, same run, same instrument: the overall\nin-process median with the daemon up is **1704.4 us over 300 samples**,\nagainst R7's 1000 us ceiling. That is RED. See `reports/R7/DENEMELER.md`\ndeneme 4.\n\n## What it means, honestly\n\nR1.3 closed this at 3.5–4.9% under a 10% ceiling, with process spawn IN the\ndenominator. The prediction written into `accept.sh` was that removing spawn\nshrinks the denominator, so the same absolute cost must read as a LARGER\npercentage. It did not grow the way that prediction implies — 4.98% sits at\nthe top of R1.3's band, not above it.\n\nThe reason is visible in the 2b number and should not be spun into good news:\nthe denominator did not shrink. The median under the daemon is 1704.4 us,\nwhich is not a post-spawn cost. `native/gated.cpp` forks TWICE per request,\nso the design that was measured re-pays a process cost the daemon was\nsupposed to delete. Until that is addressed, 2c's percentage is being taken\nagainst a denominator that still contains process creation, and it is\ntherefore NOT the re-measurement R1.3 asked for. The number is recorded\nbecause the plan requires it to be carried forward; it is not evidence that\nthe length dependence is under control.\n\nAddress named, not fixed here: `reports/R1.3/PROFIL.md:229,277` puts\n`save#2` at ~165 us and attributes the residual to `last_ledger_mode()`'s\nwhole-file fallback being O(file).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
