it would have to show up as a difference in the line\nbodies, which ARE compared. This is the smallest change that makes GOAL 3\ndecidable.\n\n**(b) Stop catting the `.head` sidecar and compare line count explicitly**,\nleaving `prev` normalised as in (a). Slightly more code, same signal.\n\n**(c) Leave it.** Then GOAL 3 stays red forever, for a reason that has\nnothing to do with whether the daemon fails SAME — and R7 cannot be accepted\nby any implementation.\n\nMy recommendation is **(a)**, in accept.sh's own commit, with the line count\nand order still compared and no other field touched. But (a) is exactly the\nmove the current ruling forbids, so it is the operator's call, not mine.\n\n## What is NOT in dispute\n\nThe 1000 us ceiling. GOAL 2b now has its first number from the sealed\ninstrument — **1704.4 us**, red — and that is a fact about the gate, not\nabout this file. Nothing here proposes touching the ceiling.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMUQjg3dw4CtQAsEVN5E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0126QCZ83bDiqmcSEQDNa5SU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nR7 tur 7: sealed run — 2a green, 2b's first sealed number is 1704.4 us (RED)\n\nApplied the operator CEVAP (a) in commit ba231d6, then ran the sealed script:\n`bash reports/R7/accept.sh > reports/R7/accept.out 2>&1` -> 10 green, 16 red\n(was 9/17).\n\n- GOAL 2a green for the first time. The diagnosis held: the failure was the\n  sleepless readiness loop, not the daemon.\n- GOAL 2b measured by the SEALED instrument for the first time: 1704.4 us\n  median over 300 samples against the unchanged 1000 us ceiling. RED, and\n  WORSE than the maker's own /tmp reconstruction (1597.3 us). Reported as\n  measured; nothing spun.\n- GOAL 2c: 4.98% length divergence, recorded in reports/R7/LENGTH.md, with\n  the caveat that the denominator still contains process creation\n  (gated.cpp:19 documents two forks per request).\n- GOAL 3: after identity normalisation, exit code, ev, mode, rule, refusal\n  text, seq and ledger line count/order are byte-identical across all three\n  commands. This is also the sealed-script confirmation of the two fail-opens\n  closed in deneme 3.\n\nNOT done, on purpose: the residual GOAL 3 divergence is the `prev` chain\nfield and the `.head` sidecar, both identity-derived and both outside the\nthree fields the operator authorised. Written up as reports/R7/CHALLENGE-2.md\nfor a separate decision; no file changed for it. GOAL 4d not written either --\nauthoring a preparation record for a two-armed run that has never happened\nwould turn a check green without the value existing.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3; timeout 120 git push -q 2>&1 | tail -3; echo \"push rc=$?\"","description":"Commit and push tur 7 results"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2289,"cache_read_input_tokens":98669,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2289},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"baed5e1f-1a03-43c7-ba0d-e3a68687202c","uuid":"40e34181-0628-40ec-b189-2edb4c790276","request_id":"req_011CeMUQiRteWUm7sNvSwK1v"}
